            <tr>
              <td>Licence</td>
              <td>MIT open-source core; paid Pro and Ultimate</td>
              <td>Proprietary; Free plan</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Where collections live</td>
              <td>Plain-text files on your disk: OpenCollection YAML (default for new collections since v3.1) or <code>.bru</code></td>
              <td>Postman cloud workspaces; with v12 <strong>Native Git</strong>, also multi-file YAML in your repo (desktop app only, sign-in required)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Account required</td>
              <td>No</td>
              <td>Yes for collections, environments, mocks and monitors. The signed-out "lightweight API Client" has none of these</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Offline / air-gapped</td>
              <td>Yes</td>
              <td>Lightweight client only</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Protocols (official pricing pages)</td>
              <td>HTTP, REST, GraphQL, gRPC</td>
              <td>HTTP, GraphQL, gRPC, WebSocket, MQTT</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Scripting</td>
              <td>JavaScript pre-request and post-response scripts, tests, declarative <code>assert</code> blocks</td>
